# What a card is for, and the pair of buttons that crosses one.
#
# Three things this is a picture of, and the first two are the same correction seen from either
# end: a card has to be a grouping rather than a border.
#
#   - Modules is fourteen rows and no headings, so it has no groups and draws none. It used to
#     come out inside a single surface, which is a box drawn round the page - it says nothing
#     about any row, because there is nothing for those rows to be grouped apart from.
#   - The Radio card's details are six groups, so they keep every card they have. The gate is
#     about sections with nothing to say, not about cards.
#   - And About is the case the cards were hiding rather than fixing. Four ungrouped rows, two of
#     them verbs: the verbs indented past a disc and the fields began at the panel's padding, so
#     the text started in two columns with a card edge between them. Every row now starts in the
#     verbs' column, the empty gutter included.
#
# Then the part that is new rather than undone. The d-pad walks rows, Left/Right are the editor's
# inside a section and L1/R1 are the tabs - so until now the cards were a grouping the eye was
# given and the thumb was not. L2/R2 move a whole group at a time.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 200
config

tab settings
hold 700

# About: four rows, one column. The two verbs carry a disc and the two fields carry the gutter.
key a
hold 1800
key b
hold 500

# Modules: no groups, so no card. Fourteen rows on the panel, with room around their symbols.
key down 12
key a
hold 2000
key b
hold 500

# The Radio card's details, on the Radio tab: About radio's readings and the verbs done to the
# radio, a card a group, and the weight lives in the discs rather than in the words. The cards'
# verbs end on the Radio card's refresh, and details is the one above it.
tab radio
key down 9
key up
key a
hold 2200

# R2 down the cards, one press per group, landing on each group's first row rather than on its
# title - the same pair on this tab as on Settings, because the page is a section.
key r2
hold 900
key r2
hold 900
key r2
hold 900
key r2
hold 1400

# And back. The first L2 goes to the top of the group the cursor is in - not out of it - which is
# what the same button does in a document reader, and what makes the pair usable with one thumb.
key down
hold 700
key l2
hold 1200
key l2
hold 900
key l2
hold 1600
